{"text": "Next, if you had a wish list it would look a lot like the following:\n1. Lease Bonus. Ask for a bonus payable at signing to cover legal fees and also the possible\ncost of removing a recorded lease from the record at termination.\n2. Pipelines. Understand the pipeline provisions. They should only be for the servicing of the\nwell and not unlimited (for example, for a transmission line for all area wells) also the pipes should\nbe sufficiently buried to allow for proper tillage and farm operations and the lessee should not\ninterfere with farm operations...\n3. Term of Lease and Delay Rentals. Term should be shorter rather than longer. Short lease\ngives incentive to lessee to drill, long lease can be used to tie up property. Also, coordinate term\nwith a delay rental (also called a \"drill or pay\") provision meaning that lessee has a period of time to\nsink a well (producing royalties) or otherwise pay rent. Also, a standard lease will usually provide for\nextension of the lease as long as oil is being produced in \"Paying Quantities\" be sure you define this\nand know what it is. Also, consider the development potential of the land.\n4. Royalties. Payment should come directly from the company purchasing the oil if possible.\n5. Shut In royalties and Duty to operate with due diligence. Landowner should get paid even if\nLessee decides not to operate well for period of time. If well is out of operation for too long, lease\nshould terminate.\n6. Location. Landowner should control location of well, storage tanks, roads, pipes, etc.\n7. Dry Hole and Continued Production. Lease should require lease to continue to drill on property\nif well is dry to fully utilize the reserve.\n8. Termination. Try to get automatic termination provisions. Sometimes lease is hard to find if\nthey aren't performing on the lease.\n9. Restoration. Land should be restored, equipment removed and well capped according to Ohio\ndept of Natural Resources Mineral Resources Management Division guidelines (this is also where a\nlease bonus helps!)\n\n10. Sale. Landowner approval of sale of lease by lease..",
